> 
> My major question first....
> 
> 	What is the point of hacking the gnomish mines? I get to
> the town at the bottom and usually get my ass kicked by the
> priest(ess) when I convert the altar. I saw something about
> luckstones but there were no real details.
> 

You're probably at too low a level to be able to defeat the
temple priest (without some heavy duty weaponry).

The mines are a great place to pick up armor and weapons early
on.  Also I use the mines as a place to read scrolls.  The bad
one to indentify early on is a destroy armor scroll.  Down in
the mines you can remove everything except for one piece and
start reading scrolls (assuming you know they're not cursed).
If you find it then all you have to do is replace what you lost.
After destroy armor, fire, and amnesia aren't too bad (just
remember to drop scrolls, spellbooks, and potions before
reading each one.  Scroll of punishment is bad but very rare.

A luckstone can be found a the bottom of the mine below the
town level.  Very useful item to carry around.  Luck is
important for many aspects of the game.

> About fountains now...
> 
> 	I never get anything by dipping in a fountain. Is it
> actually useful?
> 
Some fountains are magical and can raise stats.  Sometimes you
can uncurse items by dipping into a fountain.  And Knights have
a good time.

> Sacrificing...
> 
> 	Once I get my aligned weapon from sacrificing, as a low level
> character (<10) is there any point to sacrificing more?
> 
Sacrificing should continue to work on your prayer timeout.
Also you can get more than one artifact which is useful.

